# The binary four- and five-dimensional cases of 15.3.24

`Source.not_four_and_not_five_of_earlier` proves both exclusions from the
permitted earlier source conclusions and universal classification witnesses.
The four-dimensional branch constructs the actual module alternatives and
eliminates both repeated naturals and natural plus dual. The five-dimensional
branch constructs an outside parabolic and applies 15.3.23 and this proved
four-dimensional exclusion to its genuine smaller component.

The reduction to `LS` preserves characteristic two, the fixed Sylow subgroup,
and solvable invariant control, and identifies its local module with `⟨Z^L⟩`.
The final argument retains the original component witness without identifying
different star quotients. The module interfaces use actual conjugation on
`[W_L,L]`; the `Z_L` projection retains the exact central supplement and the
relative centralizer of `Z`. Both choices of Hypothesis 15.3.10 are preserved.

The earlier 15.3.2–17 conclusions, smaller-overgroup 15.3.15/22/23 results,
and universal B.5.1/B.4.2, I.1.6(6), and C.1.34 inputs remain explicit for
the parent Section 15.3 assembly. No L₄ or L₅ exclusion is an input to the
combined theorem.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
printed pp.1129–1130 (PDF pp.1146–1147).
-/
